// A merged module's top-level bindings are ITS OWN.
//
// A declaration merges under a qualified identity, so `Store.read` and `Cache.read` coexist. A
// binding used to keep its short name in the merged program's one flat scope, so all three `conn`s
// here — two modules' private state and this file's own — were one slot: whichever statement ran
// last silently won for everybody, and a module read a value from code that had never heard of it.
// With both immutable it surfaced instead as `cannot assign to conn, which is immutable`, pointing
// at a line whose author had bound a name they own.
//
// Each module's binding now carries that module's identity, so the three coexist, `rename` writes
// through the capture to `Store`'s own (a capture is a live view, not a copy), and this file's
// `conn` is untouched by any of it.
// expect: stdout "store cache mine"
// expect: stdout "renamed cache mine"
// expect: exit 0
use App.Store.{read as store_read, rename}
use App.Cache.read as cache_read

conn = "mine"

echo "${store_read()} ${cache_read()} ${conn}"
rename("renamed")
echo "${store_read()} ${cache_read()} ${conn}"
